{"id": "JEEM_001", "question_latex": "f(x)=\\int \\frac{(2-x^{2})e^{x}}{(\\sqrt{1+x})(1-x)^{3/2}} \\, dx. \\text{ If } f(0)=0, \\text{ then } f\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\text{ is equal to: (A) } \\sqrt{3e}+1 \\text{ (B) } \\sqrt{2e}-1 \\text{ (C) } \\sqrt{2e}+1 \\text{ (D) } \\sqrt{3e}-1", "exam": "JEE Main", "year": null, "topic": "Indefinite Integration", "difficulty": null, "source": "Top_50_JEE_Integration_PYQs_PDF.pdf, page 2, Q1"}
{"id": "JEEM_002", "question_latex": "\\text{If } \\int (\\sin x)^{-11/2}(\\cos x)^{-5/2} dx = -\\frac{p_1}{q_1}(\\cot x)^{9/2}-\\frac{p_2}{q_2}(\\cot x)^{5/2}-\\frac{p_3}{q_3}(\\cot x)^{1/2}+\\frac{p_4}{q_4}(\\cot x)^{-3/2}+C, \\text{ where } p_i,q_i \\text{ are positive integers with } \\gcd(p_i,q_i)=1 \\text{ for } i=1,2,3,4 \\text{ and } C \\text{ is the constant of integration, then } \\frac{15p_1p_2p_3p_4}{q_1q_2q_3q_4} \\text{ is equal to } \\_\\_\\_", "exam": "JEE Main", "year": null, "topic": "Indefinite Integration", "difficulty": null, "source": "Top_50_JEE_Integration_PYQs_PDF.pdf, page 2, Q2"}
{"id": "JEEM_003", "question_latex": "f(t)=\\int\\left(\\frac{1-\\sin(\\log_e t)}{1-\\cos(\\log_e t)}\\right)dt,\\ t>1. \\text{ If } f(e^{\\pi/2})=-e^{\\pi/2} \\text{ and } f(e^{\\pi/4})=\\alpha e^{\\pi/4}, \\text{ then } \\alpha \\text{ equals: (A) } -1+\\sqrt{2} \\text{ (B) } -1-2\\sqrt{2} \\text{ (C) } -1-\\sqrt{2} \\text{ (D) } 1+\\sqrt{2}", "exam": "JEE Main", "year": null, "topic": "Indefinite Integration", "difficulty": null, "source": "Top_50_JEE_Integration_PYQs_PDF.pdf, page 2, Q3"}
{"id": "JEEM_004", "question_latex": "\\text{If } \\int\\left(\\frac{1-5\\cos^{2}x}{\\sin^{5}x\\cos^{2}x}\\right)dx=f(x)+C, \\text{ then } f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\text{ is equal to: (A) } \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}(4+\\sqrt{6}) \\text{ (B) } \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(26+\\sqrt{3}) \\text{ (C) } \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(26-\\sqrt{3}) \\text{ (D) } \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}}(8-\\sqrt{6})", "exam": "JEE Main", "year": null, "topic": "Indefinite Integration", "difficulty": null, "source": "Top_50_JEE_Integration_PYQs_PDF.pdf, page 2, Q4"}
{"id": "JEEM_005", "question_latex": "I(x)=\\int \\frac{3\\,dx}{(4x+6)\\sqrt{4x^{2}+8x+3}} \\text{ and } I(0)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}+20. \\text{ If } I\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{2}}{b}+c, \\text{ where } a,b,c\\in N,\\ \\gcd(a,b)=1, \\text{ then } a+b+c \\text{ is equal to: (A) } 29 \\text{ (B) } 31 \\text{ (C) } 30 \\text{ (D) } 28", "exam": "JEE Main", "year": null, "topic": "Indefinite Integration", "difficulty": null, "source": "Top_50_JEE_Integration_PYQs_PDF.pdf, page 3, Q5"}
{"id": "JEEM_006", "question_latex": "f(x)=\\int \\frac{dx}{x^{2/3}+2x^{1/2}} \\text{ be such that } f(0)=-26+24\\log_e 2. \\text{ If } f(1)=a+b\\log_e 3, \\text{ where } a,b\\in Z, \\text{ then } a+b \\text{ is equal to: (A) } -26 \\text{ (B) } -5 \\text{ (C) } -18 \\text{ (D) } -11", "exam": "JEE Main", "year": null, "topic": "Indefinite Integration", "difficulty": null, "source": "Top_50_JEE_Integration_PYQs_PDF.pdf, page 3, Q6"}
